  "solution": "<p><strong>1.</strong> The inner modulus changes at 0. The outer one changes where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>, namely at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>. Thus split the stated interval at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>.</p><p><strong>2.</strong> The four formulas on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></mrow></math> are respectively <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>. All are nonnegative on their pieces.</p><p><strong>3.</strong> Their triangular areas are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>. The total is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>, answer D. Integrating these four linear expressions independently gives the same total.</p>"
